nancial burden of the loan, providing insight into the applicant's repayment capacity. Individuals with high monthly credit may face greater challenges in meeting loan commitments.\ndf['avg_monthly_credit'] = df['credit_amount'] / df['duration']\nend\n\npython\n# Feature name: age_group\n# Feature description: Bin the age column into groups: 'young' (18-30), 'middle-aged' (31-50), and 'senior' (51+).\n# Usefulness: Age correlates with financial stability and risk tolerance. Binning simplifies the variable into meaningful demographic categories, allowing the model to capture age-based trends effectively.\ndf['age_group'] = pd.cut(df['age'], bins=[18, 30, 50, 75], labels=['young', 'middle-aged', 'senior'])\nend\n\npython\n# Feature name: savings_status_encoded\n# Feature description: One-hot encode the savings_status categorical column.\n# Usefulness: Savings Status reflects the applicant's liquidity and financial preparedness. Encoding these statuses as binary features allows the model to distinguish applicants with varying levels of financial security.\nsavings_status_encoded = pd.get_dummies(df['savings_status'], prefix='savings_status')\ndf = pd.concat([df, savings_status_encoded], axis=1)\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column savings_status is dropped\n# The original savings_status column has been one-hot encoded into multiple binary columns, preserving its information in a format more suitable for the model.\ndf.drop(columns=['savings_status'], inplace=True)\nend\n\nThese steps generate features that improve the interpretability and predictive power of the dataset by capturing applicant behavior (average monthly credit), demographic patterns (age groups), and financial security (savings status).", "### Possible Next Three Steps:\n\npython\n# Feature name: debt_to_income_ratio\n# Feature description: Calculate the ratio of the credit_amount to the installment_commitment multiplied by 12 (approximate annual disposable income percentage).\ndf['debt_to_income